Z||000037||GT Bastard||12-12-2001||05:44 AM||||Ed is no longer able to access the forum, so he asked me I could post a message on his behalf. This is the message he typed for the forum members:<P>Dear Cliff and PFF members,<P>    Ever since Cliff booted me from the forum, things just haven't been the same.  I wake up each night in a cold sweat wishing that I hadn't been such a complete fool.  I feel that you all deserve an explaination for my queer behavior while I was still on the forum... The truth is, I have both male and female genitals.  This condition tends to wreck havock on my hormones and causes me to masturbate constantly.  Of course, having both genitals also allows me the rare oppurtunity to literally f*ck myself. My point is... It's not easy being Mr. Ed, so give me a break boys. Anyway, I hope Cliff will have a change of heart and allow me to frolic on the forum once again.  Hugs & kisses... <P>sincerely,<BR>EdsB52<P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000038||JSocha||12-12-2001||05:57 AM||||ROFLMFAO!<P>That is hysterically funny!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'd give you more smilies GT, so put each of the above to the "n" th power!<P>heheheheheheheheheheh hahahahahahahaha hohohohohohohohohoho hahahahahahahaha!||||reg||10
Z||000039||84Bill||12-12-2001||09:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B> <BR>The JSocha Ed war was a real classic!<BR>Usually JSocha is a fun friendly guy but he<BR>can slam with the best of them, very funny reading. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh man I was floored! Thats when I went out and got my Law books and new world dictionary. <BR>I had 4 scholars (2 Harvard law 1 Hindu priest and a blonde from Buffalo) decoding for a month  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000040||JSocha||12-12-2001||10:41 AM||||Have to borrow this for a moment.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Well, I just got an email from our dearest Eddie. ..... I did catch the subject though. It said: "Quit <B>sensoring!</B>" (sic - I guess he didn't have his dictionary at hand).<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  It really makes one wonder (if not me personally) who his writer really was all that time.<BR>====================<BR>Anyways...last night I was working on my fathers computer to eliminate a virus he had gotten which sent out tons of emails, and where I update his virus detection software and he is still getting "Undelivered Mail" messages from what the virus had sent out, which of course have the virus attached to them which his virus detection software is now able to recognize.  But it locks up his email client (Outlook Express 2000) when the virus come back to him.<P>So we went directly to his ISP provider and patched into his account on their server to delete the offending email messages with the virus so he could retrieve his email with his client.<P>Then I showed him how to flag all his "Junk Mail" so it heads to the DELETED folder and informed him he could also do it like we did the virus program.<P>Got home lastnight and checked my email and of course the norm, tons and tons of Junk Email with some valid emails (none of them from Ed...thank goodness).  Some have been flagged to head to my JUNK EMAIL folder (line emails from Ed) which I purge occasionaly because it has no usefull purpose to me and is just annoying.<P>This may get lengthy folks...sorry.<P>Then I started to think....I know what your all saying, thinking is bad!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon3.gif"> <P>Then it hit me like a freight train, that this in fact may have a purpose afterall!<P>Bare with me:<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>We know that there is 3000+ of us and only 1 Ed (You can do the math in a moment).<BR><LI>We know that some of this junk email comes to us with out a return email address and sometimes without the name of the sending party.  Meaning, they are keeping the fields in their email client's properties blank.<BR><LI>We know Ed is studying to become a lawyer and as he had basically mentioned in another thread, they are required to spend hours researching (he of course took the liberty of pointing that fact out to me).<BR><LI>In another thread, he mentioned how he has to defend himself all the time and doesn't have to time to read and respond because of that.<BR><LI>Most importantly, ISP's will close an account if that account is suddenly bombarded which is tying up their server space.<BR></UL><P>So, here is just another butt fart that I had and of course, for me it is still early.<BR><OL TYPE=1><BR><LI>We collect all this unsoliceted email and place it in a Junk Folder for later retrievel.<BR><LI>We coordinate and pick a day and syncronize a time to one time zone to compensate for the many time zones.<BR><LI>The day before, we adjust our email properties so that it does not send out our names and/or our return email addresses with any emails.<BR><LI>We all select the junk mail and flag it to FORWARD to Ed but we save it in our DRAFTS folder so it is ready.  I myself can personally forward, oh?, 3 maybe 4 thousand junk emails myself.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><LI>On the date and time we all agree upon, we move them from the DRAFTS folder to our respective email clients OUTBOX and hit the Send/Receive button and send the EMAILS to Ed, swamping his email account.<BR><LI>We also set that every "X" days, we will send him another batch.<BR></OL><P>This will give Ed pleanty of stuff to read and since we aren't sending him electively a) Our Names and/or b) Our return email message in any way, he couldn't respond back to us.<P>Just some food for thought or for the toilet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
